From cf37dc0466f07f6c61c15373575c07c87dc5fdb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rasheed <arasheedu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:46:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] trace: forward runner events and gate layer/sample
 steps in llama-server

Adds the API llm uses to pass on events a patched llama-server produces:
Forward (detail-filtered against the schema's EVENT_DETAIL), StepStartAt,
Now and the runner capability flag that request.received reports.

t_ns is now assigned under a per-request lock and never goes backwards in
seq order, so rebased runner timestamps cannot reorder the stream.

In layer/sample step mode the Go token gate is off and acks are queued for
llama-server's POST /trace/ack instead; DisableRunnerStep falls back to the
token gate for a stock runner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
